odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:30977:A soft page break is a page break that has been included in a document by a page-oriented consumer at a position where the document itself does not include a page break as defined by fo:break-after 20.184 or fo:break-before 20.185. 
odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:37495:The fo:border, fo:border-top, fo:border-bottom, fo:border-left and fo:border-right attributes specify border properties for these elements:
